    <edge source="Ständerat" target="Nationalrat">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Nationalrat and Ständerat collaborate in the legislative process, convening separately for discussions and jointly in the Vereinigte Bundesversammlung.&lt;SEP&gt;Both the Ständerat and Nationalrat legislate together, treating constitutional amendments and laws that must be approved by both houses.</data>
      <data key="d9">collaborate,convene,legislate</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ständerat" target="Kanton">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Ständerat represents the interests of the cantons in the Swiss Federal Assembly, although it does not have direct instructions from them.</data>
      <data key="d9">represent</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ständerat" target="Kantonsvertretung">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Ständerat functions under the concept of Kantonsvertretung, although it is stated that members are not legally obligated to represent their cantons or take instructions from them.</data>
      <data key="d9">function</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ständerat" target="Instruktionsverbot">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Ständerat operates under the principle of Instruktionsverbot, which ensures that its members maintain autonomy in decision-making, independent of external pressures.</data>
      <data key="d9">guided by</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ständerat" target="Parlament">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Council of States also constitutes one of the two key chambers within the Swiss parliament.</data>
      <data key="d9">is part of</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kanton" target="Landsgemeinde">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">In some cantons, governance is facilitated through the Landsgemeinde, which serves as the highest legislative body for direct public involvement.</data>
      <data key="d9">govern</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kanton" target="Gericht">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Each Kanton includes various types of Gerichte, serving different legal functions.</data>
