      <data key="d8">Certain Kantons include spezialverwaltungsgerichte for specific administrative cases.</data>
      <data key="d9">includes</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-004</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kanton" target="Jugendgerichte">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Several Kantons contain Jugendgerichte that deal with youth issues.</data>
      <data key="d9">contains</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-004</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kanton" target="Strafgericht">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">In certain Kantons, the Strafgericht replaces the Bezirksgericht or Obergericht for serious criminal cases.</data>
      <data key="d9">replaces</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-004</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kanton" target="Kassationsgericht">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Some Kantons previously included a Kassationsgericht until 2011.</data>
      <data key="d9">previously included</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-004</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kanton" target="Verfassungsgericht">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Kantons of Basel-Stadt, Geneva, and Jura have established a Verfassungsgericht for constitutional matters.</data>
      <data key="d9">has</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-004</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nationalrat" target="Parlament">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The National Council functions as one of the two chambers within the Swiss parliament structure.</data>
      <data key="d9">is part of</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vereinigte Bundesversammlung" target="Bundesrat">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Vereinigte Bundesversammlung is responsible for electing members of the Bundesrat, as well as the Bundespräsident and other federal officials.</data>
      <data key="d9">elect</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Bundespräsident">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Bundesrat collectively leads the Swiss executive government, while the Bundespräsident is elected from its members to preside among equals.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bundesrat elects one of its members to the position of Bundespräsident for a one-year term.</data>
      <data key="d9">election,lead</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Vizepräsident">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Bundesrat elects one of its members to the role of Vizepräsident for a one-year term, often following the term of the Bundespräsident.</data>
      <data key="d9">election</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Bundeskanzlei">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Bundesrat is responsible for the functioning and decision-making processes in conjunction with the Bundeskanzlei.</data>
      <data key="d9">responsibility</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Guy Parmelin">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Guy Parmelin is a member of the Bundesrat representing the canton of Vaud and holds the position of Bundespräsident for 2026.</data>
      <data key="d9">membership</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Ignazio Cassis">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Ignazio Cassis is a member of the Bundesrat representing the canton of Ticino and serves as the Vizepräsident for 2026.</data>
      <data key="d9">membership</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Karin Keller-Sutter">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Karin Keller-Sutter is a member of the Bundesrat representing the canton of St. Gallen.</data>
      <data key="d9">membership</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Albert Rösti">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Albert Rösti is a member of the Bundesrat representing the canton of Bern.</data>
      <data key="d9">membership</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Elisabeth Baume-Schneider">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Elisabeth Baume-Schneider is a member of the Bundesrat representing the canton of Jura.</data>
      <data key="d9">membership</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Beat Jans">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Beat Jans is a member of the Bundesrat representing the canton of Basel-Stadt.</data>
      <data key="d9">membership</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Martin Pfister">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Martin Pfister is a member of the Bundesrat representing the canton of Zug.</data>
      <data key="d9">membership</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Regierungsrat">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Bundesrat functions similarly to the Regierungsrat at the federal level in Switzerland.</data>
      <data key="d9">similarity</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Staatsrat">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Bundesrat functions similarly to the Staatsrat at the cantonal level in Switzerland.</data>
      <data key="d9">similarity</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Standeskommission">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Bundesrat functions similarly to the Standeskommission in Appenzell Innerrhoden at the cantonal level.</data>
      <data key="d9">similarity</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesrat" target="Schweizerische Eidgenossenschaft">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Bundesrat acts as the executive governing body of the Schweizerische Eidgenossenschaft, overseeing national matters.</data>
      <data key="d9">governs</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundespräsident" target="Schweizer Regierung">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The President of the Swiss Confederation represents the Swiss government in official matters.</data>
      <data key="d9">represents</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kantonsvertretung" target="Volksvertretung">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Distinguishes the representation of the general populace in the National Council from that of cantons in the Council of States.</data>
      <data key="d9">distinguishes</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Schweizerische Eidgenossenschaft" target="Föderalismus">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Describes the federal structure and autonomy of cantons within the Swiss Confederation.</data>
      <data key="d9">characterizes</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Föderalismus" target="Direkte Demokratie">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Enables direct involvement of citizens in government through democratic mechanisms within the framework of federalism.</data>
      <data key="d9">enables</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Föderalismus" target="Bundesverfassung">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Bundesverfassung describes the principles of Föderalismus in Switzerland.</data>
      <data key="d9">describes</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-004</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Direkte Demokratie" target="Volksrechte">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Correlates the implementation of citizen rights with direct democratic practices.</data>
      <data key="d9">rooted in</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Direkte Demokratie" target="Urnengang">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The voting process is integral to the functioning of direct democracy in Switzerland.</data>
      <data key="d9">integral to</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Gewaltenteilung">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Ensures the respect for citizen rights through independent government structures as defined by the principle of separation of powers.</data>
      <data key="d9">ensures</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Schweizer Demokratie">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Swiss democracy involves the Volksrechte, empowering citizens to actively participate in the political process.</data>
      <data key="d9">influences,involves</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Bundesverfassung">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Volksrechte require a popular vote for amendments to the Bundesverfassung, thus impacting its content and structure.</data>
      <data key="d9">impacts,requires</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Referendumsrecht">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Referendumsrecht empowers the Volksrechte by allowing the electorate to challenge and confirm parliamentary decisions.</data>
      <data key="d9">allows,empowers</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Wahlrecht">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Wahlrecht grants citizens the right to vote, enabling them to exercise their Volksrechte in elections.</data>
      <data key="d9">enables,grants</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Stimmrecht">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Stimmrecht affords the electorate the opportunity to influence government proposals, thus allowing the exercise of Volksrechte.</data>
      <data key="d9">affords,allows</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Kantonale Rechte">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The kantonale Rechte extend the Volksrechte, providing more comprehensive forms of participatory governance at the cantonal level.</data>
      <data key="d9">enhance,extend</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Gesetzesinitiative">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Gesetzesinitiative enables citizens to propose legislative changes as an expression of the Volksrechte.</data>
      <data key="d9">enables,proposes</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Finanzreferendum">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Finanzreferendum governs financial expenditures, determining the Volksrechte citizen participation in fiscal matters.</data>
      <data key="d9">determines,governs</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksrechte" target="Stimmberechtigte">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Stimmberechtigte are empowered by the Volksrechte, which encompass the rights to vote and participate in the democratic process.</data>
      <data key="d9">empowered by,include</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-005</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gewaltenteilung" target="Subsidiarität">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The principle of subsidiarity interacts with the separation of powers in organizing governance decisions at appropriate levels.</data>
      <data key="d9">interrelates with</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesversammlung" target="Schweizer Regierung">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Swiss Federal Assembly comprises the Swiss government as part of its structure.</data>
      <data key="d9">comprises</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799658</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bund" target="Parlament">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Federation encompasses the structure and function of the parliament in the Swiss political system.</data>
      <data key="d9">includes</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="schweizerische Bundesverfassung" target="Kantone">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Swiss Federal Constitution provides the legal structure for the autonomy and governance of the cantons.</data>
      <data key="d9">framework for</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kantone" target="Bezirke">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The cantons include districts as part of their administrative organization, though districts lack political autonomy.</data>
      <data key="d9">includes</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksvertretung" target="Interpellation">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The parliamentary procedure of interpellation is used by the popular representation to question the government.</data>
      <data key="d9">utilizes</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksvertretung" target="Motion">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Motions are adopted by the popular representation to direct actions from the government.</data>
      <data key="d9">adopted by</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Volksvertretung" target="Postulat">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Postulates are used by the popular representation to request government investigations on specific issues.</data>
      <data key="d9">used for</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-67a86848d7820be81a8cc7885716f2f2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1784799659</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bundesverfassung" target="Volksinitiative">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Volksinitiative allows citizens to propose changes to the Bundesverfassung, linking citizen initiatives to constitutional alterations.</data>
      <data key="d9">changes,proposes</data>
